  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/geoff-williams-fellowship-in-physics-n-a-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics",
      "description": "Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics - N/A, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia Education & Training Level B Fixed term - Full-time Level B Add to favourites View favourites Based in School of Chemistry, Physics and Earth Science, City East campus Full-time fixed term contract for 3 years, with potential for extension Salary Range: (Level B) $117,100 - $138,515 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Join the Geoff William’s Fellowship and develop your career as a teaching and research-focused academic in Experimental Physics. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Following a generous donation, the School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences is pleased to invite applications for the Lecturer (Level B) – Geoff William Fellowship in Physics. This Fellowship is designed to support an emerging academic with strong research and teaching potential and provide the opportunity to build a rewarding career in Physics. The Fellowship offers the opportunity to develop as a well-rounded academic, with a strong focus on both research and teaching. Ideally, the successful candidate will contribute to the University’s growing research strengths in Quantum Materials, Solid State Physics and Quantum Technologies, an area of significant investment at Adelaide University, supported by new laboratories, infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration. We will also welcome applications from candidates in broader fields such as astrophysics, photonics, particle, nuclear and radiation physics, or another relevant area aligned with the discipline of physics. You will undertake experimental and/or theoretical research, contribute to the development of future teaching opportunities in areas relevant for Quantum Materials such as solid-state physics, and build collaborative networks that help advance the field of physics. The team Reporting to an Academic Lead, you’ll be part of the Physics Discipline within the School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences. You’ll collaborate with internationally connected research groups and receive mentoring from a senior academic in Physics. Our researchers contribute to discoveries shaping the future of energy, health, resources and the environment, with impact extending locally and globally. This research excellence informs our teaching, equipping students with strong scientific foundations and practical skills through access to advanced laboratory facilities. Visit the AU website to learn more about School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for a researcher who thrives in a collaborative and intellectually curious environment. You’ll work alongside researchers and academics across diverse areas of experimental and theoretical physics, with opportunities to strengthen your teaching, develop research collaborations and contribute to the continued growth and impact of the discipline. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Qualifications A PhD in Physics, or equivalent higher degree, awarded within the last 8 years in an area that aligns with the existing and emerging strengths of Physics at Adelaide University Experience Demonstrated research expertise in quantum materials, astrophysics, photonics, particle, nuclear and radiation physics, or another relevant area aligned with the discipline Demonstrated ability, relative to opportunity, to conduct independent research that aligns with an existing or emerging strengths in Physics at Adelaide University Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research in addition to working effectively as a member of a team in a complex setting. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. A strong interest in undergraduate and graduate education in Experimental Physics. Demonstrated experience in grant writing and research funding applications, including the ability to develop compelling funding proposals, articulate research objectives and impact, and contribute to successful applications for competitive research funding. Commitment to the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 10 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493390 ) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) fbe44061 Last Name (required) 4d327efa Email (required) 0b90d1d9 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) d55d6eec Last Name (required) b72a2d04 Email (required) c7e210d5 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Practice Design and Improvement Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead practice design and process improvement to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, operating models and controls across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 5ee0c860 Last Name (required) c445bea7 Email (required) 2a3d