    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/director-roseworthy-veterinary-hospital-roseworthy-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Director, Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital",
      "description": "Director, Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital - Roseworthy, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Director, Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 HEO10 Management Continuing - Full-time HEO10 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in College of Science, Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital at the Roseworthy Campus Lead a World-Class Veterinary Teaching Hospital | Drive Innovation, Excellence and Impact Full-time, continuing position At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Adelaide University is seeking an exceptional leader to become the next Director of Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital (RVH). This is a rare opportunity to lead a large-scale veterinary teaching hospital at the intersection of education, professional practice, research, and community service. Work that matters As Director, you will provide strategic, people-focused and influential leadership, guiding a high performing clinical enterprise that delivers outstanding veterinary care while supporting the next generation of veterinary professionals. You will inspire multidisciplinary teams, drive growth, foster innovation, and strengthen partnerships. Provide strategic and people-focused leadership, guiding a high-performing, financially sustainable clinical teaching enterprise at the forefront of veterinary education and professional practice. Working across the University and with key stakeholders, the role will shape and deliver Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital’s strategic direction, building on its strengths and identifying opportunities for growth, innovation and impact. In this role, you will foster a culture of excellence, collaboration and continuous improvement, ensuring the hospital delivers outstanding clinical services while providing an exceptional learning environment for veterinary students and professionals. With a strong focus on education, clinical excellence, innovation and community engagement, the role will contribute directly to Adelaide University’s strategic ambitions and strengthen Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital’s position as a leading centre for veterinary teaching, practice and applied innovation. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Executive Director, College of Science, you will be a member of the College Professional leadership team and lead the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital. The role is based at our extensive Roseworthy campus, home to South Australia’s only veterinary school and the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital, which provides 24/7 veterinary services to the community. Visit the Adelaide University website to learn more about the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who thrives in leading a passionate multidiscipline team, shaping future directions and making a meaningful impact. You will thrive in a collaborative, purpose-driven environment focused on innovation, excellence and positive outcomes. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated success in senior people leadership roles, leading multidisciplinary teams A proven ability to build positive workplace cultures and developing people to achieve their potential Experience driving business growth, financial sustainability and organisational performance Extensive experience in strategic and business planning, leading and sustaining innovation, continuous improvement and effective service delivery Demonstrated expertise in people management, wellbeing and safety, budgeting and financial management, and strategic planning and policies and governance frameworks Outstanding stakeholder engagement, communication, and negotiation skills Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter addressing your suitability for the position, including specific reference to the following requirements: Experience driving business growth, financial sustainability and organisational performance Extensive experience in strategic and business planning, leading and sustaining innovation, continuous improvement and effective service delivery Demonstrated expertise in people management, wellbeing and safety, budgeting and financial management, and strategic planning and policies and governance frameworks Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 3 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493564) : Jessica Maslen Team Lead, Talent Acquisition, People & Culture +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV144