      "title": "Exhibitions Coordinator",
      "description": "Exhibitions Coordinator - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training HEO6 Continuing - Full-time HEO6 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in MOD. at the City West Campus Full-time (1.0 FTE), continuing position Salary Range (HEO6) $94,269 - $101,828 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Reporting to the Manager, Exhibitions and Experience Design, the role will be responsible for developing exhibitions and programs by generating ideas, researching current themes, and contributing to the selection and design of exhibits that communicate science, technology, engineering, mathematics, and complex research to the public. Curious to learn more? Are you excited by ideas and creating experiences that matter? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role works closely with internal stakeholders including the MOD. Team, AU academics and also closely with external stakeholders like our Youth Board, artists, designers and developers. Visit the AU website to learn more About Us - MOD Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys variety and meeting new people. You will experience a range of tasks and interactions, keeping your workday interesting and engaging. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven ability delivering complex creative projects on time, to budget, and to a high quality Proven ability in strong analytical and research skills, with excellent writing and editing abilities Proven ability to network and communicate with diverse stakeholders, including those from a range of cultural backgrounds Experience working cooperatively with people at various organisational levels Experience in graphic design, visual communication, or exhibition design, supported by knowledge or programming of relevant technologies and software development, and experience delivering digital or technology-related projects for public audiences. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application 