    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/accounts-receivable-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Accounts Receivable Officer",
      "description": "Accounts Receivable Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance HEO4 Continuing - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in Corporate Portfolio on North Terrace Full-time continuing position This role forms part of the Finance Team, providing professional service delivery At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Working as part of a collaborative team, the successful incumbent will process and administer accounts receivable services for the University, supporting the accurate and timely processing of invoicing, receipting and management of revenue collection across research, sundry and student debtors. The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Finance Operations team within the Finance Function and is aligned to the Corporate Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys variety and meeting new people. You will experience a range of tasks and interactions with stakeholders across the University, keeping your workday interesting and engaging. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrates active listening and questioning skills to identify customer/stakeholder needs Demonstrated problem solving and analytical skills Proven ability to work collaboratively within a team-based operational environment Experience in debt management Demonstrated ability to promote the organisational values and a commitment to positively comply with the associated behaviour expectations Experience using ServiceNow, Peoplesoft, Microsoft Office including Word and Excel Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Sunday 25 October 2026. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493542) Hinnd Ahmadie Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 85c9bad7 Last Name (required) 97eeb94b Email (required) 60e4d635 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 5c2ff316 Last Name (required) 5434bb3a Email (required) 1ea6bc46 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Practice Design and Improvement Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead practice design and process improvement to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, operating models and controls across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) a7c6e987 Last Name (required) 464aecbe Email (required) 145c9d47 Job Alert e737d093 Finalize y