    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/quality-and-compliance-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Quality and Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Quality and Compliance Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Quality and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO5 Human resources Fixed term - Full-time HEO5 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in in People & Culture at the City West Campus Three Full-time 12-month fixed term contract opportunities Salary Range: $84,498 - $93,955 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Make a meaningful impact by helping ensure a fair, compliant and high-performing workplace. As a Quality and Compliance Officer, you'll safeguard employee records, support critical compliance activities, deliver trusted advice, and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives that strengthen how people and culture services are delivered across the University. Your work will help create confidence, integrity and positive outcomes for staff, managers and the wider university community. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team These roles sit within the Quality and Compliance function aligned to the People and Culture Portfolio. Working closely with People Services and Careers, Legal, Risk, data and analytics teams, senior leaders, and external regulatory bodies, the team provides trusted advice on complex compliance matters, support audit activities, monitor legislative changes, and helps embed consistent, compliant practices across the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about People & Culture. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This is an opportunity for detail-oriented professionals to make a real impact by supporting critical compliance activities, maintaining data integrity, and delivering trusted advice that helps ensure a positive employee experience across the University. We're looking for proactive and solutions-focused professionals to help drive operational excellence through audits, compliance monitoring, record management and process improvement. Your work will directly contribute to a trusted, compliant and high-performing workplace. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience delivering operational administration, compliance or audit-related services within a complex organisational environment Experience applying policies, procedures, industrial requirements and compliance frameworks to support service delivery Proven ability to maintain accurate records and ensure data integrity across business systems Proven ability to manage competing priorities and meet service delivery targets Proven ability to manage sensitive and confidential information with discretion and in accordance with privacy and records management requirements Proven ability to communicate effectively with a range of stakeholders and provide clear, customer-focused advice and support Proven ability to identify process improvement opportunities, contribute to service enhancement initiatives and escalate complex matters appropriately Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter the online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 18 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493545) : Emma Kelvin – Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 0482 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) a2567221 Last Name (required) fa202bd9 Email (required) 44278ef7 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 5c9ec829 Last Name (required) b763b026 Email (required) d8940734 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community 