    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-business-analyst-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-5153d481-6e3b-4ad3-b589-ee96e112cd0d": {
      "title": "Senior Business Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Business Analyst - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO8 Human resources Fixed term - Full-time HEO8 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in People & Culture at City West Full-time, fixed term contract until 30 June 2028 Salary Range: $116,320 - $130,498 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As Senior Business Analyst, you will lead the analysis, design and improvement of pay accuracy and entitlement processes across Adelaide University. Working closely with payroll, workforce administration, technology and business stakeholders, you will translate remediation findings, audit outcomes and compliance requirements into practical improvements that strengthen processes, controls and system workflows. You will map current and future-state processes, identify root causes and opportunities for simplification, automation and standardisation, and develop sustainable operating models that support compliant, efficient and consistent service delivery. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Join a team delivering meaningful change for our people. The Pay Accuracy and Entitlements Program brings together experts across project management, governance, payroll, compliance, employee relations, change, and education to strengthen payroll practices, enhance compliance, and improve employee outcomes. The Senior Business Analyst is a key role in delivering process and system changes, including business requirements, testing, implementation and change readiness. Through strong stakeholder engagement, process analysis and problem-solving skills, the role will provide practical advice and develop clear documentation, controls and guidance that support informed decision-making, continuous improvement and consistent pay and entitlement practices. Visit the AU website to learn more about People & Culture. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who brings strong problem-solving skills, attention to detail and a continuous improvement mindset, along with the ability to build relationships, communicate clearly and influence stakeholders at all levels. Someone who is comfortable working collaboratively across teams and turning complex issues into practical, sustainable improvements. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience undertaking senior business analysis and leading end-to-end process redesign and business transformation within large, complex organisations Strong capability in requirements elicitation, process modelling and operating model design Experience working within payroll, HR, workforce management, compliance or highly regulated operational environments Proven ability to identify root causes, assess operational risks and implement sustainable process and control improvements Experience applying Lean, Six Sigma, Business Process Management or similar methodologies Advanced analytical and problem-solving skills, including experience using complex operational data to inform business improvements Proven ability to provide advice and influence senior leaders and cross-functional stakeholders to deliver effective change Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11: 30pm Sunday 25 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493578 ): Jessica De Lorenzo Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 5eedc5f5 Last Name (required) c0c4c094 Email (required) 40c99b4a Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) e923bfb9 Last Name (required) 5083755e Email (required) 1956c51f Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Practice Design and Improvement Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead practice design and process improvement to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, operating models and controls across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 3608b821 Last Name (required) 5ffb6416 Email (required) 910ac682 Job Alert 0cb0ff5b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO8 Human resources HEO8 Human resources Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People and Culture People and Culture Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
