    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/practice-design-and-improvement-lead-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Practice Design and Improvement Lead",
      "description": "Practice Design and Improvement Lead - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Practice Design and Improvement Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO9 Human resources Fixed term - Full-time HEO9 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in People & Culture at City West Full-time, fixed term contract until 30 September 2028 Salary Range: $135,226 - $144,672 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Lead the design and implementation of future-state pay accuracy and entitlement practices that strengthen compliance and help prevent future underpayments across Adelaide University. As the leader of the Practice Design and Improvement workstream, you will lead a team focused on continuous improvement, operating model design and end-to-end process transformation, turning audit, remediation and discovery findings into practical, sustainable solutions. You will drive the development of frameworks, standards, controls and processes that support accurate payment outcomes and embed stronger practices into business-as-usual operations. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Join a team delivering meaningful outcomes for our people. In this role, you will partner with business leaders, Payroll, Employee Relations, HR and IT to deliver complex process and system improvements across the employee lifecycle, with an initial focus on high-risk employment arrangements and payment practices. Visit the AU website to learn more about People & Culture. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who thrives on leading complex transformation and continuous improvement, with a strong understanding of process design, operating models and compliance. You’ll be skilled at turning audit, remediation and risk findings into practical, sustainable improvements, and confident working across people, process and technology. If you’re a strong stakeholder manager who can influence senior leaders and lead large-scale change, you’ll be well suited to this opportunity. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Leading business transformation, operating model design or continuous improvement initiatives within a complex organisation. Demonstrated experience translating compliance, audit or remediation findings into sustainable operational improvements. Proven ability to lead large-scale process redesign and implementation programs. Working with payroll, workforce management, HR or related compliance environments. Strong stakeholder engagement and influencing skills, including working with senior leaders. Experience managing cross-functional projects involving technology, people and process change. Delivery of a Practice Design and Improvement workstream, ensuring governance, reporting, risk management and implementation activities achieve sustainable and measurable outcomes. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11: 30pm Thursday 22 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493579 ): Jessica De Lorenzo Team Lead, Talent Acquisitions +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 7ef18f72 Last Name (required) 8167ef24 Email (required) 43afd907 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) edc3ae50 Last Name (required) 1852e6f5 Email (required) 00f69147 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 6f4fa401 Last Name (required) 4e1486e1 Email (required) a56c5592 Job Alert 927cbebb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO9 Human resources HEO9 Human resources Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People and Culture People and Culture Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
