    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/veterinarian-clinician-gp-small-animal-hospital-roseworthy-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Veterinarian Clinician (GP), Small Animal Hospital",
      "description": "Veterinarian Clinician (GP), Small Animal Hospital - Roseworthy, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Veterinarian Clinician (GP), Small Animal Hospital Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 Education & Training HEO8 Continuing - Full-time HEO8 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based at the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital, Roseworthy Campus Full-time (1.0 FTE), continuing position Salary Range (HEO 8): $116,320 - $130,498 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) plus Shift loadings where applicable. Be part of a supportive teaching hospital offering professional development opportunities and access to specialist expertise and mentoring. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it's a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia's future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As a Veterinary Clinician, you’ll provide high-quality GP care to small animal patients, with opportunities to be involved in Emergency & Critical Care (ECC). No two days will be the same as you work alongside experienced specialists to manage a diverse range of cases and deliver evidence-based patient care. Working in a teaching hospital means we offer you more than a clinical role. You will have the opportunity to provide real-world learning experiences for veterinary students, helping them develop the skills and knowledge to become confident, capable veterinarians. Longer consultation times allows you time to thoroughly investigate complex cases, collaborate with specialist teams and deliver excellent clinical outcomes. Part of a broader multidisciplinary hospital, we offer Small Animal, Large Animal and Pathology services, with specialist expertise across Orthopaedics, Oncology, Anaesthesia, ECC and General Practice. You’ll have access to advanced diagnostic equipment including ultrasound, X-ray and CT, a dedicated radiographer and an on-site Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Hospital Director, you will join the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital's Small Animal Hospital, a collaborative team providing GP, referral and emergency veterinary services. Working alongside experienced specialists, veterinary nurses and support staff, you will contribute to exceptional patient care while supporting the University's teaching and research mission. Visit the Adelaide University website to learn more about the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a supportive, hands-on clinical environment where every day brings something different. You’ll work alongside experienced specialists, care for a diverse small animal caseload, and play an important role in mentoring the next generation of veterinary professionals. With opportunities for professional development and ongoing learning, you’ll be supported to grow your clinical expertise while making a meaningful contribution to animal care, student education and the broader veterinary profession. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU. Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Veterinary qualification with registration or eligibility to be registered as a veterinarian in South Australia Experience providing GP veterinary services for companion animals Experience of high level written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills including the ability to work effectively with a diverse range of clients and team members. Proven ability to contribute to service quality and continuous improvement Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Monday 9 November For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493364 ) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #S-DNI #LI-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) db1830c9 Last Name (required) 690c6d5b Email (required) 63c6623c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 74229cf1 Last Name (required) 398f6773 Email (required) 65a026d8 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) cab5b510 Last Name (required) d4a2659c Email (required) 5fe6c892 Job Alert 8c4cfde8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education & Training HEO8 Education & Training HEO8 Locations Roseworthy, SA, Australia Roseworthy, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Science College of Science Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn