    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-manager-research-compliance-and-ethics-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Research Compliance and Ethics",
      "description": "Senior Manager, Research Compliance and Ethics - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Manager, Research Compliance and Ethics Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO9 Management Fixed term - Full-time HEO9 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Research and Innovation Portfolio in the Adelaide CBD Full-time, 13-month fixed term contract HEO9 ($135,226 - $144,672) + 17% Superannuation At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Lead and manage a high performing team of subject matter experts and deliver expert advice and support to University senior staff, researchers, regulators, and other stakeholders to enable research activities to be conducted with integrity and in compliance with all applicable regulatory or policy requirements. The role oversees specialist support for the University’s research compliance and ethics committees (Institutional Biosafety Committee, Animal Ethics Committees, and Human Research Ethics Committees). Working closely with stakeholders in the Research Services and Infrastructure Function, the role supports education on research compliance and ethics and ensures institutional compliance within complex ethical and regulatory frameworks. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of the Research Compliance, Ethics and Integrity team within the Research Services and Infrastructure Function and is aligned to the Research and Innovation Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about Research and Innovation Portfolio Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience leading and managing high performing multidisciplinary teams in research compliance, and ethics Proven ability in research management and administration, with a focus on research ethics and compliance Comprehensive understanding of current legislation, regulations, standards, guidelines, and codes of practice relating to human research ethics, animal ethics, biosafety or biosecurity Proven ability to provide high-level interpretation and advice on policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements Experience in interpersonal, presentation, communication, and advisory skills, with the capacity to work collaboratively and influence across organisational boundaries Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you are interested in this role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Tuesday 20 October 2026. Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493541): Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 2a672a9c Last Name (required) 3c1b510f Email (required) f7b3ca7c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 64f5809f Last Name (required) 773d9cf1 Email (required) 30b64f2e Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 1dacf889 Last Name (required) 61647a5b Email (required) 129363aa Job Alert d77514d7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO9 Management HEO9 Management Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio Research and Innovation Research and Innovation Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
