    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/associate-director-strategic-projects-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-4bb32151-ea8a-43c4-a72e-9e43924e4093": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Strategic Projects",
      "description": "Associate Director, Strategic Projects - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Associate Director, Strategic Projects Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO10 Management Continuing - Full-time HEO10 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in International and External Engagement at the City West campus Full-time, continuing position Salary Range: $149,351 – $159,177 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Associate Director, Strategic Projects is responsible for leading the governance, implementation and delivery of strategic initiatives and transformational programs across the International and External Engagement portfolio. The role provides high-level strategic analysis, project leadership and operational coordination to drive portfolio priorities, ensure effective execution of key objectives, and support the successful delivery of organisational outcomes. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team The International and External Engagement portfolio advances Adelaide University’s vision through strategic partnerships, global engagement, brand leadership, student recruitment and philanthropy. By fostering strong relationships with industry, government, communities, alumni and international partners, the portfolio enhances the University’s reputation, expands its impact, and supports its position as Australia’s most industry-engaged university. Visit the AU website to learn more about International and External Engagement. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Extensive experience leading complex strategic initiatives, transformation programs and cross-functional projects within a large and complex organisation, delivering outcomes through influence, collaboration and effective stakeholder engagement Strong analytical and problem-solving capability, including the ability to assess complex issues, identify implementation risks and opportunities, and develop practical recommendations that support successful delivery of strategic priorities Demonstrated success managing the end-to-end delivery of strategic programs, including planning, implementation, monitoring, risk management and benefits realisation Strong experience leading organisational change, continuous improvement and transformation activities, including managing competing priorities and delivering outcomes in ambiguous and evolving environments Highly developed stakeholder engagement, negotiation and influencing skills, with a demonstrated ability to build productive relationships across portfolios, functions and external partners to achieve agreed outcomes Significant experience maintaining governance frameworks, strategic planning implementation and executive reporting Proven ability to lead multidisciplinary teams and project resources, fostering collaboration, accountability and a high-performance culture focused on delivery and continuous improvement Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 25 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493393) Alexandra Koszegi Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
