    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/research-associate-in-statistics-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Statistics",
      "description": "Research Associate in Statistics - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Research Associate in Statistics Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Add to favourites View favourites Based in Australian Centre for Precision Health, located at the SAHMRI campus Full-time, 2 -year fixed term contract Make a positive impact within the School of Public Health At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters You will contribute to research addressing some of today's most important public health challenges, including healthy ageing, chronic disease prevention, and cognitive health. Your work will involve analysing large-scale genomic and population health data to advance scientific understanding and inform strategies that support healthier lives and better health outcomes. Supported by NHMRC Investigator Grant funding, this role offers the opportunity to make meaningful contributions to research with real-world impact while working at the forefront of epidemiology and precision health. The team This position sits within the Nutritional and Genetic Epidemiology Group at Australian Centre for Precision Health, reporting directly to Professor Elina Hypponen. You will join a multidisciplinary team of researchers, working with experts in epidemiology, biostatistics, genomics, and machine learning. We offer a collaborative environment, access to world-class data resources, and excellent opportunities for publication and career development. Visit the AU website to learn more about Australian Centre for Precision Health Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. We expect that you will thrive in a collaborative research environment while also demonstrating the initiative, organisation, and independence needed to manage your own work effectively. We value individuals who are curious, eager to learn new methods and techniques, and committed to continuous professional development. As a member of our team, you will build strong working relationships with colleagues from a range of disciplines, contribute to a supportive and inclusive culture, and play an important role in maintaining a reliable and high-performing research environment. Together, we strive to foster excellence, innovation, and mutual support in the pursuit of impactful health research. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Essential Postgraduate qualifications in epidemiology, statistics, genetics, statistical genomics or a related discipline. A developing track record of peer review publications, commensurate to opportunity Proven high-level problem-solving and organizational skills to manage competing demands and meet project timelines. Demonstrated analytical skills with experience on epidemiological and/or genetic association analyses. High-level written communication skills with the ability to present information effectively and clearly to a wide audience and a variety of stakeholders, especially writing for publication. Demonstrated experience and ability to work collaboratively as part of a diverse and multi-disciplinary research team as well as work independently. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30 pm Friday 30 October 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact ( quoting reference number 493515): Taryn Giles Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/research-associate-mawson-lakes-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate - Mawson Lakes, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Research Associate Mawson Lakes, SA, Australia, 5095 Education & Training Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Add to favourites View favourites Based in the College of Engineering and Information Technology at the Mawson Lakes Full-time, 12 month fixed term contract Salary Range: $ 103,962 - $111,384 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Contribute to the development of the next generation of operational forest inventory technologies At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters This multidisciplinary project will require a highly motivated postdoctoral research associate who will help to develop the next generation of operational forest inventory methods. The project combines unmanned aerial laser scanning (ULS), terrestrial and mobile laser scanning (TLS/MLS), statistical calibration-transfer, and machine learning technologies to improve the estimation of forest structural attributes across plantation forest environments. Building on recently developed methods for LiDAR fusion and calibration-transfer, the successful applicant will investigate new approaches for transferring detailed structural information from limited ground-based LiDAR acquisitions to landscape-scale aerial datasets. The research will contribute to scalable forest inventory systems supporting timber valuation, carbon accounting, forest monitoring, and precision forest management. Curious to learn more? The team Based in Mawson Lakes, you'll be part of a collaborative team working closely with the Forestry Centre of Excellence at Adelaide University's Mount Gambier campus. Developed in partnership with industry, this project is focused on delivering practical research and innovative solutions that directly address the challenges facing the forestry sector. The Green Triangle is Australia's premier forestry region, producing around one-third of the country's structural timber. Through strong partnerships with industry, government and research organisations, you'll contribute to the development of cutting-edge technologies that improve decision-making across the forest value chain and support the sustainability and growth of Australia's timber industry. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Forestry Centre of Excellence . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. The successful applicant will contribute to research including: development of next-generation calibration-transfer and domain adaptation methods for multi-platform LiDAR machine learning and statistical modelling of forest structural attributes (e.g., DBH, height, crown dimensions, biomass, and stem quality) uncertainty quantification and propagation in operational forest inventory development of transferable inventory models across species, sites, stand age, sensors, and geographic regions automated tree detection, segmentation, and structural reconstruction scalable processing pipelines for large point-cloud datasets integration of aerial, terrestrial, and mobile LiDAR with other sensing modalities publication of high-impact journal papers and collaboration with forestry industry partners Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: a PhD (or be close to completion) in Remote Sensing, Computer Vision, Forestry, Geomatics, Machine Learning, Spatial Statistics, or a closely related discipline demonstrated research experience in one or more of: LiDAR processing forest inventory photogrammetry machine learning computer vision geospatial analysis experience analysing large spatial datasets programming experience in Python, R, or MATLAB strong quantitative and statistical skills excellent written and oral communication skills Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter the online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address Submit your application by 11:30pm Thursday 22 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493558 ) : Emma Kelvin – Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 0482 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-animal-technician-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-1e250ba9-5838-492d-a3ae-ba51f824017f": {
      "title": "Senior Animal Technician",
      "description": "Senior Animal Technician - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Animal Technician Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO4 Fixed term - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in Biological Services, Research and Innovation North Terrace Campus Full-time, 38-month fixed-term contract Salary range: $75,366 to $82,607 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Support the expanding research programs of the South Australian immunoGENomics Cancer Institute (SAiGENCI) through the provision of high-quality daily animal care, welfare monitoring, and breeding colony management. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Team Lead and embedded in Biological Services, this fixed term position is funded by SAiGENCI, an independent cancer-focused medical research institute embedded within Adelaide University. The role provides dedicated support for SAiGENCI research while also contributing to broader facility operation. The team provides animal care and technical support that enables biomedical research across the University. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. You will work closely with technicians, researchers, students and facility users in a practical environment where careful animal care, collaboration and sound judgement matter every day. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: A tertiary qualification in a relevant field with relevant work experience, or an equivalent combination of experience and training. Biomedical research animal husbandry, including breeding and barrier or Specific Pathogen Free (SPF) practices. Technical procedures such as injections, venepuncture, biopsies and post-operative care. Familiarity with Animal Ethics Committee (AEC), Institute Biosafety Committee (IBC) and associated facility procedures. The ability to create and maintain accurate written and electronic records. Work health and safety, infection control, sterilisation and aseptic techniques in animal facilities. Support researchers through training in animal handling and facility protocols, while ensuring equipment and supplies are prepared and readily available for operational needs. You must hold a valid Australian driver’s licence. Evening, weekend and public holiday work, including roster participation, may be required. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 18 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493510) : Georgia Borg Talent Acquisition Advisor +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DN I Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/tern-ecosystems-processes-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "TERN Ecosystems Processes Officer",
      "description": "TERN Ecosystems Processes Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me TERN Ecosystems Processes Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO5 Fixed term - Full-time HEO5 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the College of Science at the City East campus Full-time, fixed term contract until 31 December 2028 Salary Range: $88,989 - $100,268 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Contribute to ecosystem research through fieldwork, data management and equipment support At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Make a meaningful contribution to understanding and protecting Australia’s ecosystems. As a TERN Ecosystem Processes Officer, you will support vital environmental research through field monitoring, scientific data collection and remote sensor operations. Working across diverse and often remote landscapes, you will help generate the high-quality data that informs research, environmental management and future conservation outcomes. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team Join the Terrestrial Ecosystem Research Network (TERN), Australia's ecosystem observatory and a nationally significant research infrastructure supporting environmental science across the country. TERN provides the data, monitoring platforms and research infrastructure that help scientists understand how Australia's ecosystems are changing over time and respond to environmental challenges such as climate change, biodiversity loss and land management pressures. As part of this collaborative and purpose-driven team, you'll contribute to nationally important research while working in some of Australia's most unique and diverse environments. Visit the AU website to learn more about TERN. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. The ideal candidate is a self-motivated, hands-on and adaptable field professional with a passion for environmental research and a strong commitment to safety, quality and teamwork. They bring experience supporting field-based scientific projects, maintaining monitoring equipment and collecting high-quality environmental data in diverse and sometimes remote environments. Remote work will include 1-2 day trips twice per month with teams of postgraduate students, staff and lab groups. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience supporting environmental monitoring, scientific fieldwork or research activities in field-based environments Demonstrated experience operating, maintaining and troubleshooting scientific monitoring equipment, including coordinating equipment servicing and maintaining associated procedures and documentation Demonstrated experience collecting, managing and quality checking environmental or research data using relevant digital tools and systems Experience with programming and scripted data analysis, together with a willingness to learn new technical skills that support environmental monitoring activities Demonstrated knowledge of health, safety and risk management practices, including experience supporting compliance activities within a research, laboratory or field-based environment Proven ability to organise, prioritise and coordinate activities to achieve objectives and meet deadlines in remote or complex operating environments Demonstrated experience communicating professionally and building effective working relationships with academics, students, researchers and external stakeholders to achieve project outcomes Demonstrated experience undertaking fieldwork in remote or challenging environments Demonstrated experience with soil and vegetation sampling methodologies and specimen preparation techniques Experience In addition, some special requirements for the preferred candidate for this role are included below; This role may involve travel locally or nationally This role may involve manual handling, working at heights or in confined spaces You must hold a valid Australian driver’s licence You must hold, or be willing to obtain and maintain, a current first aid qualification relevant to remote field operations Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter the online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address Submit your application by 11:30pm Wednesday 21 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact quoting reference number 493401 Emma Kelvin – Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 0482 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 57253a7e Last Name (required) 6785c1c6 Email (required) 029b9096 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 9204a78e Last Name (required) 45c57f2e Email (required) 1bf9d603 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 5469274a Last Name (required) 9d4a3940 Email (required) d9a62a2c Job Alert f8c47c63 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO5 HEO5 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Science College of Science Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
