    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/casual-small-animal-veterinary-nurse-opportunities-emergency-critical-care-roseworthy-veterinary-hospital-roseworthy-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Casual Small Animal Veterinary Nurse Opportunities",
      "description": "Casual Small Animal Veterinary Nurse Opportunities - Emergency Critical Care – Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital - Roseworthy, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Casual Small Animal Veterinary Nurse Opportunities - Emergency Critical Care – Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 HEO4 Casual HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Casual Small Animal Veterinary Nurse Opportunities - Emergency Critical Care – Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital $49.30 per hour plus roster penalties and shift loadings, which may equate to approximately 30–40% above hourly rate depending on roster participation At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. Join the Small Animal Veterinary Nurse - Emergency Critical Care team at the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital in a casual capacity, providing support on an ad hoc basis as operational needs arise. This role is ideal for someone seeking flexible work, with shifts offered as required to cover periods of increased demand, staff leave and other operational requirements. Shifts may include weekdays, evenings, nights and weekends. Work that matters As a Small Animal Veterinary Nurse - Emergency Critical Care you will play a key role in patient monitoring and care, anaesthesia and imaging preparation, emergency triage and stabilisation, treatment implementation, and client communication, while also contributing to clinical teaching and mentoring support for veterinary students in a collaborative hospital environment. Working closely with veterinarians, client relations, and administrative teams, you will support safe and effective clinical delivery across medical, surgical, dental, diagnostic, and emergency services while contributing to the smooth operation of the hospital through best-practice hygiene, animal housing, and biosecurity standards. This is a casual opportunity with shifts offered as operational needs arise, providing flexibility while contributing to a dynamic clinical and teaching environment. About Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital (RVH) is the School's clinical teaching facility and comprises small and large animal hospitals and a veterinary diagnostic laboratory. As a leading primary care, referral and 24/7 emergency veterinary hospital, RVH delivers high-quality veterinary services across a broad range of animal species using state-of-the-art facilities and technology. The hospital also provides an exceptional clinical learning environment, where final-year veterinary medicine and veterinary technology students gain practical experience under the guidance of experienced veterinarians, nurses and professional staff. Core Responsibilities Deliver professional and compassionate customer service to clients in person, over the phone and via email. Manage appointment bookings, patient admissions and discharges, and general reception enquiries. Liaise with referring veterinary practices and support communication between clients and clinical staff. Assist with emergency presentations and patient handling as required. Maintain accurate patient records using veterinary practice management software. Process payments, invoices and insurance claims. Contribute to maintaining a welcoming, organised and professional reception environment. Provide administrative support to ensure the efficient day-to-day operation of the hospital. Essential Skills and Experience Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing, or a Bachelor of Veterinary Technology, together with a minimum of two years’ relevant veterinary nursing experience. Experience in veterinary nursing with sound technical skills in areas such as surgery, emergency, internal medicine or general practice Experience working in a clinical setting maintaining best practices Experience with practice management software Experience providing supervision and/or training to students Experience applying Occupational Health and Safety and biosecurity protocols Experience working independently and as part of a team in a dynamic hospital environment Ability to participate in a 24/7 rotational roster Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. This is a casual opportunity with shifts available as operational needs arise, offering flexibility and the opportunity to support a dedicated team delivering exceptional veterinary care. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia and for the term of appointment. To be eligible, you will need to reside within Australia. This will remain open until all roles are filled. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493517) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 3786fe55 Last Name (required) 2a2eac48 Email (required) 5b0d45c3 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 05dec581 Last Name (required) ca38af2b Email (required) e0986179 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geoff Williams Fellowship in Physics N/A, SA, Australia School of Physics, Chemistry and Earth Sciences Build your academic career through physics research, teaching, mentoring and collaboration across leading research programs. Exhibitions Coordinator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Community and Regional Engagement This role forms part of Museum and Cultural Institutions team within the Community and Regional Engagement Function and is aligned to the International and External Engagement Portfolio within the University. Accounts Receivable Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance The role supports effective financial administration through consistent payment receipting and compliant receivables processing and adherence to university policies and procedures. Senior Business Analyst Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead process improvement and transformation to strengthen pay accuracy, compliance, controls and sustainable business practices across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 4a50af19 Last Name (required) 3dd3448e Email (required) 98a6cb14 Job Alert 958bbf0e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO4 HEO4 Locations Roseworthy, SA, Australia Roseworthy, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Science College of Science Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
