    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/associate-director-business-development-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-44a195e2-6832-4ae2-9a4a-9c7609aa1037": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Business Development",
      "description": "Associate Director, Business Development - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Associate Director, Business Development Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO10 Continuing - Full-time Position Description Based in the Research and Innovation Portfolio Full-time, continuing position Salary Range: $149,351 - $159,177 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Make a meaningful impact on Adelaide University’s partnered research in Health and Medical Innovation At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Associate Director, Business Development will provide leadership to a high-performing team, driving business development, industry engagement and strategic partnerships aligned with Adelaide University’s priorities. The role will be responsible for managing an implementing strategic business development plans, revenue pipelines and industry engagement strategies. The Associate Director will oversee major proposals, funding opportunities, contract negotiations and partnership development, while providing strategic advice on business planning, financial performance, risk management and governance. Through strong stakeholder engagement, team leadership and a focus on continuous improvement, the role will promote the University’s research capabilities, strengthen strategic alliances and enhance Adelaide University’s reputation as a partner of choice. To succeed in this role, you will need a strong strategic and proactive mindset, driven by desire to deliver impact. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team The Associate Director, Business Development forms part of the Research Business Development and Alliances team within the Research and International Translation Function and is aligned to the Research and Innovation Portfolio within the University. This role will provide role guidance, professional development, direction and coaching for up to 3 direct reports. You will work closely with leaders and staff, senior academics and professional staff, industry and government partners, research networks and academic collaborators. Visit the AU website to learn more about Research and innovation | Adelaide University Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys variety and meeting new people. You will experience a range of responsibilities and interactions, keeping your workday interesting and engaging.  In this role, you will thrive in a collaborative, purpose-driven environment, driving innovation, research translation and sustainable growth while strengthening Adelaide University’s industry engagement and reputation. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven ability leading and developing high-performing teams in business development or research translation Experience developing and delivering strategic business development plans, commercial contracts, and partnership programs Experience building and managing relationships with industry, government, and research collaborators Experience in financial analysis, contract management, and risk assessment Experience preparing and securing major proposals, bids, and tenders for research funding and alliances Experience communicating and engaging with diverse stakeholders Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Sunday 1 November 2026. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493576) : Jessica Maslen Team Lead, Talent Acquisition, People & Culture +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications are welcomed from Australian citizens, residing in Australia only. Appointment is subject to a Personnel Security Clearance at NEGATIVE VETTING LEVEL 1 being obtained and maintained. Pursuant to the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (the Act) and the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Regulations 2019 (the Regulations), this position has been deemed prescribed. This role will require the successful candidate to hold #S-DNI #LI-DNI Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer -  Mechanical Engineering Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering Lead innovative mechanical engineering research and teaching, build industry partnerships and develop the next generation of engineering professionals. Senior Manager, Category Management Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance Drive strategic procurement, shape enterprise category strategy and deliver meaningful commercial outcomes in this full time, continuing Senior Manager position in the Procurement team. Research Officer - Climate Resilient Sheep Systems Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 School of Animal and Veterinary Sciences Support agricultural research projects by coordinating field activities, collecting and analysing data, and assisting with research operations across South Australia. University Veterinarian Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Infrastructure This role provides expert leadership in animal health and welfare, ethics, and compliance across research and teaching activities at Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
