    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-mechanical-engineering-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer -  Mechanical Engineering - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Lecturer -  Mechanical Engineering Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Engineering Level C Continuing - Full-time Based in the School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering, College of Engineering and Information Technology, City East Campus Full-time, continuing position Salary range: (Level C): $142,789 to $151,354 per annum, plus 17% superannuation. Join a leading engineering school with opportunities to collaborate across disciplines, build industry partnerships and contribute to world-class research and teaching. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering is seeking an outstanding Senior Lecturer to contribute to teaching and research within the school. You will drive high-quality research, deliver engaging and innovative teaching, and foster strong industry and research partnerships to address complex engineering challenges and achieve meaningful outcomes for society. We welcome applicants with expertise in areas including advanced materials and structures, biomechanics, thermodynamics and fluid mechanics, dynamics and control systems, and sustainable engineering and renewable energy, with demonstrated experience in teaching relevant subjects. You will also bring a strong record of high-quality research publications, the ability to attract competitive and industry research funding, and experience developing collaborative partnerships. In addition, you will contribute to curriculum and course development using evidence-based teaching practices, supervise postgraduate research students to successful completion, and support research leadership, team development and University engagement activities. The team Reporting to the Academic Lead, Associate Professor Rey Chin, you will work alongside academic colleagues, students, industry partners and research organisations to advance engineering research and education. You will contribute to research leadership, competitive funding, postgraduate supervision, curriculum development and the continued growth of the School’s research profile. Visit the Adelaide University website to learn more about the School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This opportunity is ideal for academics who are passionate about advancing mechanical engineering through research, teaching and collaboration. You will be part of a diverse and dynamic academic environment, with opportunities to collaborate across disciplines, engage with industry and external research partners, supervise postgraduate researchers and contribute to the development of future engineering professionals. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Qualifications PhD in Mechanical Engineering, or closely related engineering discipline, with expertise in a recognised specialisation. Experience Substantial record of research achievements as evidenced by publications in high-quality journals or conference proceedings that are considered prestigious by peers. Demonstrated ability to win significant research funding through competitive and industry funding programmes. Demonstrate expertise to achieve national recognition through independent and innovative contributions to research in the discipline. Substantial record of success in effective teaching and course coordination using evidence-based pedagogy that promotes student engagement. Lead teams in evidence-based design and development of learning activities, assessments and content, at the course level. Demonstrated ability to attract and supervise postgraduate students to successful completion. Ability and willingness to engage with industry or external research organisations. Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 17 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 492605 ) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #S-DNI #LI-DNI Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Business Development Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Services Lead and manage strategic business development to drive new funding opportunities, revenue generation and enhance Adelaide University’s reputation as the partner of choice across Health and Medical Innovation research areas. Senior Manager, Category Management Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance Drive strategic procurement, shape enterprise category strategy and deliver meaningful commercial outcomes in this full time, continuing Senior Manager position in the Procurement team. Research Officer - Climate Resilient Sheep Systems Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 School of Animal and Veterinary Sciences Support agricultural research projects by coordinating field activities, collecting and analysing data, and assisting with research operations across South Australia. University Veterinarian Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Infrastructure This role provides expert leadership in animal health and welfare, ethics, and compliance across research and teaching activities at Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
