    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-manager-category-management-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Category Management",
      "description": "Senior Manager, Category Management - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Manager, Category Management Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance HEO9 Continuing - Full-time HEO9 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Coach and develop high-performing procurement professionals Technology and professional services category experience will be highly regarded Full-time continuing opportunity at Adelaide University Salary range: $135,226 - $144,672 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Role Summary Lead enterprise category management, complex sourcing and strategic supplier partnerships to deliver value, innovation and responsible procurement outcomes across Adelaide University. Work that matters As Senior Manager, Category Management, you will lead enterprise-wide category planning, complex sourcing initiatives and manage strategic supplier relationships that deliver long-term value for Adelaide University. Reporting to the Director, Procurement, you will influence senior stakeholders, coach and develop high-performing procurement professionals, and help embed best-practice procurement, sustainability, risk management and commercial excellence across the institution. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Director, Procurement, this senior role sits within the Procurement team in the Finance Function. You will work closely with senior leaders, procurement colleagues and stakeholders across the University to shape category strategies, navigate complex commercial decisions and deliver outcomes that support institutional priorities, financial sustainability, innovation and operational excellence. Visit the AU website to learn more about Finance and Procurement . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role will suit a commercially astute and collaborative procurement leader who enjoys shaping strategy, building trusted relationships and turning complex challenges into practical outcomes. You will bring credibility with senior stakeholders, a commitment to coaching and developing procurement professionals, and the judgement to balance strategic ambition with disciplined delivery. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Postgraduate qualifications in procurement, business, commerce or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education Extensive experience managing complex procurement categories and strategic sourcing initiatives in a large or complex organisation Proven ability to translate organisational priorities and market insights into category strategies that deliver measurable commercial value, service and outcomes Strong executive stakeholder engagement, supplier relationship management and negotiation and influencing skills Substantial leadership experience in procurement or category management, including coaching and developing high-performing procurement professionals Sound experience managing procurement risk, governance and compliance while enabling timely, commercially pragmatic decisions Experience leading technology and professional services categories will be highly regarded Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now! Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 27 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493534 ) Amra Delibasic Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) f543b3b1 Last Name (required) 3b20a733 Email (required) ab87c140 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 1b5fe5ad Last Name (required) dc580264 Email (required) e6e4da06 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Business Development Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Services Lead and manage strategic business development to drive new funding opportunities, revenue generation and enhance Adelaide University’s reputation as the partner of choice across Health and Medical Innovation research areas. Senior Lecturer -  Mechanical Engineering Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering Lead innovative mechanical engineering research and teaching, build industry partnerships and develop the next generation of engineering professionals. Research Officer - Climate Resilient Sheep Systems Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 School of Animal and Veterinary Sciences Support agricultural research projects by coordinating field activities, collecting and analysing data, and assisting with research operations across South Australia. University Veterinarian Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Infrastructure This role provides expert leadership in animal health and welfare, ethics, and compliance across research and teaching activities at Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 1c8235d6 Last Name (required) a6beccb6 Email (required) c0a40b09 Job Alert c1cb5fce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Finance HEO9 Finance HEO9 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio Corporate Corporate Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility