    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/research-officer-climate-resilient-sheep-systems-roseworthy-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Research Officer",
      "description": "Research Officer - Climate Resilient Sheep Systems - Roseworthy, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Research Officer - Climate Resilient Sheep Systems Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 Farming, Animals & Conservation HEO5 Fixed term - Full-time Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the College of Sciences, School of Animal and Veterinary Science at the Roseworthy Campus Full-time, 24-month fixed-term contract Salary Range: $84,498 to $93,955 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Climate Resilient Sheep Systems project aims to improve the resilience and productivity of sheep in low-rainfall farming systems. Led by Adelaide University and Murdoch University, in collaboration with researchers, farmers and industry partners across Australia, the project focuses on developing practical solutions to strengthen the sustainability of sheep and pasture systems under drought conditions. As a Research Officer, you will play a hands-on role in this important research, supporting fieldwork and farm trials across South Australia. Your responsibilities will include collecting and measuring data from livestock and plant species, establishing and maintaining pastures and shrub plantings, monitoring livestock health and welfare, and maintaining research equipment and accurate project records. You will also contribute to data collation, progress reports and project milestone documentation to support the successful delivery of the project. This varied role offers the opportunity to contribute to research addressing key challenges facing the agricultural industry, helping develop practical approaches to improving agricultural productivity and climate resilience in Australia's low-rainfall farming regions. Learn more about the Climate Resilient Sheep Systems project . Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to Associate Professor William van Wettere, you will work within the Davies livestock Research centre in the School of Animal and Veterinary Science, collaborating with academic staff, students and external research partners. Visit the AU website to learn more about Davies Livestock Research Centre and The School of Animal and Veterinary Science. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys a mix of outdoor fieldwork, practical livestock care, plant care and maintenance, and research activities. You will work collaboratively across farm trials and research settings, with opportunities to develop your technical skills, contribute to innovative agricultural research and engage with a diverse range of colleagues and external partners. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven ability in providing support for research projects, ensuring timely delivery of high-quality outcomes and adherence to project objectives Experience managing laboratory and field-based experiments Experience working with livestock, in particular sheep Knowledge of pastures and / or plants Experience coordinating data collection and analysis Proven ability to collaborate with academic teams and students, offering technical support to facilitate research activities and enhance learning outcomes Experience preparing research reports and documentation Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Thursday 29 October 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493625 ) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 931e5040 Last Name (required) 427dced6 Email (required) 8ff68aeb Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) abab0465 Last Name (required) 13d629f7 Email (required) 769699cd Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Business Development Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Services Lead and manage strategic business development to drive new funding opportunities, revenue generation and enhance Adelaide University’s reputation as the partner of choice across Health and Medical Innovation research areas. Senior Lecturer -  Mechanical Engineering Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering Lead innovative mechanical engineering research and teaching, build industry partnerships and develop the next generation of engineering professionals. Senior Manager, Category Management Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance Drive strategic procurement, shape enterprise category strategy and deliver meaningful commercial outcomes in this full time, continuing Senior Manager position in the Procurement team. University Veterinarian Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Infrastructure This role provides expert leadership in animal health and welfare, ethics, and compliance across research and teaching activities at Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) b11c677a Last Name (required) 31ec71d7 Email (required) 34575ad7 Job Alert 97108850 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Farming, Animals & Conservation HEO5 Farming, Animals & Conservation HEO5 Locations Roseworthy, SA, Australia Roseworthy, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Science College of Science Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
