    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/research-fellow-a-phosphorus-and-potassium-fertilisers-waite-urrbrae-sa-australia-adelaide-cbd": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (A)",
      "description": "Research Fellow (A) - Phosphorus and Potassium Fertilisers - Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Research Fellow (A) - Phosphorus and Potassium Fertilisers Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 Education & Training Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Based in School of Agriculture, Food and Wine at the Waite Campus Full-time fixed term contract until February 2031 Salary Range: (Level A) $103,962 - $111,384 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Work at the forefront of sustainable agriculture, collaborating with leading research and industry partners to develop innovative fertiliser technologies with real-world impact for farmers in Australia and internationally. Join a collaborative research team developing next-generation fertiliser technologies for improved phosphorus and potassium crop nutrition. Conduct laboratory and glasshouse experiments to improve crop performance and support the development of scalable, commercial solutions for farmers. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters We are seeking a Research Fellow to contribute to a multi-party funded fertiliser project, in partnership with the Grains Research and Development Corporation (GRDC), The Mosaic Company (USA) and Omnia Specialties Australia. The project aims to develop more efficient fertiliser technologies that improve crop performance and deliver better agricultural and environmental outcomes in Australia and internationally, with a focus on products that can be scaled up and commercialised for farmers. You will join a collaborative research team formulating phosphorus and potassium fertilisers, investigating, and optimising their release kinetics in different soils and uptake by crops while examining their behaviour under varying storage and handling conditions. The role will involve laboratory and glasshouse-based experimentation, advanced technical methods, data analysis and interpretation, as well as presenting research findings to industry partners and the broader agricultural sector. Curious to learn more about the project? Explore the GRDC’s Nitrogen mission The team Reporting to Roslyn Baird, Director, Fertiliser Technology Research Centre (FTRC), you will be part of a collaborative and multidisciplinary research environment, working alongside researchers, students and industry partners to deliver impactful research for the efficient delivery of nutrients to crops and the sustainability of agricultural systems. Visit the AU website to learn more about The School of Agriculture, Food and Wine. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working in a collaborative research environment and is passionate about the chemistry of fertilisers and the role of nutrient efficiency in sustainable agriculture. This laboratory and glasshouse-based research role also offers industry engagement and collaboration with the broader agricultural sector. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Qualifications a PhD in chemistry, chemical engineering, material science or soil chemistry or have equivalent qualifications. Experience Evidence of contribution towards research relevant to the chemical behaviour of phosphorus or potassium fertilisers and/or soil related compounds. Experience in laboratory and glasshouse based experimental design, including statistical analysis and interpretation of data. Experimental operation of advanced laboratory and technical equipment to enhance research outcomes Experience in collaborating with a team of researchers, external industry partners and colleagues. Excellent verbal and written communication skills and ability to present research to industry partners and the wider agricultural sector. Ability to supervise support staff and research students. Commitment to the principles of equity, diversity and inclusion, and ability to contribute to the diversity of the school community. Understanding of Wellbeing and Safety principles and practices especially related to laboratory chemicals. Desired Experience in nanotechnologies and/or mechanochemical synthesis methods. Experience in fertiliser chemistry and fertiliser behaviour in soils. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Thursday 12 November 2026 Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493527 ) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #S-DNI #LI-DNI Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Business Development Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Research Services Lead and manage strategic business development to drive new funding opportunities, revenue generation and enhance Adelaide University’s reputation as the partner of choice across Health and Medical Innovation research areas. Senior Lecturer -  Mechanical Engineering Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering Lead innovative mechanical engineering research and teaching, build industry partnerships and develop the next generation of engineering professionals. Senior Manager, Category Management Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Finance Drive strategic procurement, shape enterprise category strategy and deliver meaningful commercial outcomes in this full time, continuing Senior Manager position in the Procurement team. Research Officer - Climate Resilient Sheep Systems Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 School of Animal and Veterinary Sciences Support agricultural research projects by coordinating field activities, collecting and analysing data, and assisting with research operations across South Australia. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/administration-support-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Administration Support Officer",
      "description": "Administration Support Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Administration HEO4 Fixed term - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Student Experience and Success portfolio at the City East Campus Full-time, fixed term until 26 July 2027 Salary Range: $75,366 – $82,607 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) The Administration Support Officer position is an identified position for an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidate At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Reporting to the Manager, First Nations Student Support you will provide professional administrative and operational support across the Portfolio, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders. You will coordinate day-to-day operations, meetings, events and projects; maintain systems, records and financial administration; prepare reports and documentation; and support compliance with policies, legislation and governance requirements. You will also contribute to a collaborative, customer-focused team culture while handling sensitive information with confidentiality and discretion. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role will work closely with staff and management across the Student Experience and Success portfolio and various internal and external stakeholders. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Student Experience and Success | Adelaide University. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys variety, connecting with new people and making a positive difference. You’ll have the opportunity to work with a diverse range of people while providing exceptional service and support to students, staff and stakeholders.  You will experience a range of tasks and interactions, keeping your workday interesting and engaging. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience in providing high-level administrative support in a customer-oriented environment Proven organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities High-level interpersonal and communication skills, with experience liaising with diverse stakeholders Experience in financial administration, records management, and the use of Microsoft Office and information systems Ability to work independently and as part of a team, maintaining confidentiality and professionalism Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter explaining your interest and suitability for the role Applications for this role close at 11:30pm Wednesday 11 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493514): Jessica Maslen Team Lead, Talent Acquisition | People and Culture +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Pursuant to Section 56 part 2 of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (as amended) (SA) applications are invited from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people only. The University seeks to redress the under-representation of Aboriginal Peoples in the University through targets set within our Reconciliation Action Plan and Aboriginal Employment Action Plan and this is an equal opportunity special measure under Section 65 of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (as amended) (SA). Applicants must be of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander descent Pursuant to the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (the Act) and the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Regulations 2019 (the Regulations), this position has been deemed prescribed. This role will require the successful candidate to hold a current Working with Children Check. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 71a6ceb0 Last Name (required) c608d88d Email (required) d84598db Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) a7a93a3b Last Name (required) 5791c576 Email (required) c4bea6ab Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Stores Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Exciting opportunity to contribute to a dynamic team supporting education, research and operational excellence. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 2a4fe568 Last Name (required) 80e87d76 Email (required) 3ce6f84c Job Alert 5624999e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration HEO4 Administration HEO4 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio Student Experience and Success Student Experience and Success Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Pref