    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-software-engineer-enterprise-service-management-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management)",
      "description": "Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO8 Information Technology Continuing - Full-time Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in IT Enterprise Service Management team at the City / Mawson Lakes Campus Full-time, continuing position Salary Range: $116,320 - $130,498 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Senior Software Engineer (ESM) will provide senior technical expertise and technical leadership in the design, development and delivery of ServiceNow solutions that support enterprise service management across Adelaide University. The role will be responsible for developing secure, scalable and maintainable workflows, automation and integrations, resolving complex technical issues, contributing to platform architecture and design decisions, and providing technical direction, guidance and mentoring to developers and other technical team members. The role requires a minimum of five years’ demonstrated hands-on ServiceNow development and platform engineering experience, ideally within large and complex enterprise environments. Candidates will require strong expertise in ServiceNow solution design, JavaScript, workflow automation, integrations, platform configuration and development standards. The role will also contribute to technical governance, solution and code reviews, platform standards, management of technical debt and ensuring solutions remain maintainable and upgradeable. The role can be primarily based at either City or Mawson Lakes campus, with flexible working-from-home arrangements available in accordance with University policy. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of the IT Research Enablement & Digital Business, Enterprise Service Management team within the Information Technology Function and is aligned to the Corporate Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who combines strong hands on ServiceNow development and platform engineering expertise with curiosity and a drive to continuously improve. You’ll be comfortable developing, configuring, integrating and troubleshooting solutions yourself while also contributing to technical design and supporting others. Experience with AI, intelligent automation and applying AI capabilities to improve service delivery and user experience is highly regarded, together with strong problem solving, communication and collaboration skills. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Minimum of five years’ hands-on experience designing, developing and supporting ServiceNow solutions within large and complex enterprise environments, with strong expertise in platform configuration, JavaScript, workflow automation, integrations, security and scalable and maintainable solution design. Ability to translate complex business requirements into innovative, secure and maintainable ServiceNow solutions, with strong experience in workflow automation and enterprise integrations. Experience applying AI, intelligent automation or ServiceNow AI capabilities to improve service delivery and user experience will be highly regarded. Senior technical leadership experience within a ServiceNow environment, including providing technical direction and mentoring to developers, leading or contributing to solution and architecture decisions, undertaking technical and design reviews, resolving complex platform issues, and working collaboratively with business stakeholders, architects, technical teams and vendors. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11: 30pm Sunday 8 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493618) : Jessica De Lorenzo Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) e1f1832c Last Name (required) 255e549d Email (required) 05983ec2 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) d8d1dcf8 Last Name (required) dead53aa Email (required) c3408236 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Stores Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Exciting opportunity to contribute to a dynamic team supporting education, research and operational excellence. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 5c7f5c4a Last Name (required) 4fc4b9ef Email (required) b68a1165 Job Alert e6d46af9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO8 Information Technology HEO8 Information Technology Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio Corporate Corporate Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
