    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/teaching-casuals-au-online-2027-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Teaching Casuals (AU Online)",
      "description": "Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Casual Campaign Education & Training Casual Casual rates apply At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? We are seeking educators with specialist knowledge and skills to teach in the following fields: Business & Law Creative Arts, Design and Humanities Education, Behavioural and Social Sciences Engineering and Information Technology Health Science With degrees spanning a wide range of programs, Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. About Adelaide University Online Adelaide University Online (AUO) offers a range of 100% online degrees and aspires to be the best online education provider in Australia. Our programs are delivered across two distinct models: 10-week periods delivered over 4 terms per year 6-week periods delivered over 6 terms per year Targeted at busy adults who need to juggle work, life and family commitments, AUO is making it possible for more people to integrate study into their busy lives and pursue their career goals. Each degree has been specifically designed for online learning and is delivered in an engaging and flexible way. Students can access academics and study support out of hours and on weekends, so they can get help when they need it. Application Process: Please view the available courses through the application form, to determine what area of work offerings are being made available for individual. Ensure you meet the essential criteria – essential skills and experience listed below. Note: This is a fully remote, flexible role with work conducted primarily outside standard Monday to Friday, 9am-5pm office hours. Core Responsibilities Undertake online teaching as part of the AUO teaching team Apply disciplinary expertise to consult, facilitate discussions, mark assessment items, and provide feedback to students Implement approaches that maximise the student experience and learning outcomes Provide academic support, mentoring and advice to students Act as the first point of response/contact in managing student issues or complaints Essential Skills and Experience Minimum Bachelor’s degree and relevant professional/industry work experience (10-week courses) Minimum Masters or PhD (6-week courses) Ability to undertake a range of teaching duties in an online environment Ability to actively engage and educate a diverse student group Excellent written and interpersonal skills Ability to use the necessary digital techniques and tools required for effective online teaching Available to work outside of normal working hours, including weekends Please contact Academic and Program Services at auoacademic.programservices@adelaide.edu.au if you have any questions about this process. Please note, this email is for enquiries only. Applications will only be accepted through the online portal. Please note - By registering on the Casual/Sessional Staff Register, it does not guarantee that employment will be offered. If you already hold a casual contract with Adelaide University, please register and complete the application form to be considered for future opportunities. Registering is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV your conferred PhD Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia and for the term of appointment. To be eligible, you will need to reside within Australia. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. #S-DNI #LI-DN Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Stores Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Exciting opportunity to contribute to a dynamic team supporting education, research and operational excellence. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/common-core-opportunities-casual-semester-1-2027-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Common Core Opportunities (Casual)",
      "description": "Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Casual Campaign Casual Casual rates apply Add to favourites View favourites At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. This Registration of Interest (RoI) process is for applicants wishing to be considered for work in the Common Core by way of issuance of a casual contract. Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Opportunities for Adelaide University staff employed in continuing and fixed-term positions are offered through negotiated workload release arrangements (rather than casual contract) and are being managed via a separate process . Work that matters The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Embedded within every year of undergraduate study, the Common Core provides students with opportunities to explore contemporary issues, engage with diverse perspectives, and develop the capabilities needed to thrive in professional, civic, and global contexts. It is an industry-informed, interdisciplinary learning experience that invests in the human qualities most valued by employers and communities alike: curiosity, creativity, critical thinking, self-leadership, and collaboration. Selecting a Common Core course from one of six knowledge areas enables students to broaden their perspectives and build capabilities that complement their chosen degree. For more information about the Common Core, please visit our webpage . We seek experienced, curious, and passionate folk to join our Semester 1 2027 Common Core Teaching Teams. These are vibrant communities of practice that support peer learning, innovation, and foster a shared commitment to student success. What do our Commons Workshop Facilitators do? Our Facilitators: Lead activity- and discussion-based workshops that promote participation, inquiry, collaboration, and student-led learning. Foster a safe, respectful, and welcoming space where diverse perspectives are valued and students feel confident contributing. Tailor approaches to accommodate different backgrounds, abilities, confidence levels, and emerging student needs. Use questioning, discussion, and real-world examples to help students analyse complex issues, evaluate evidence, navigate ambiguity, and develop practical solutions. Bring curiosity, flexibility, and a willingness to learn, drawing on relevant experience and experimenting with new approaches to enhance student learning. In each of our courses, students work through a carefully curated set of materials on our course sites before attending a 2-hour Commons Workshop. Our workshop activities are designed to support curiosity, creativity and informed risk-taking through carefully scaffolded experiences and formative feedback opportunities. Common Core courses use a Non-Graded Pass model to create a learning environment focused on curiosity, exploration, and growth. Students are encouraged to take intellectual risks, engage with diverse perspectives, reflect on their learning, and develop the capabilities needed to leverage their learning in the course. Our Common Core Courses are: An Ethically Rich Life (CORE X001) Fact or Fiction: Data for Everyone (CORE X002) Igniting Change: Ideas to Action (CORE X003) Transforming Learning through First Nations Knowledges (CORE X004) Responsible AI: Bridging Ethics, Education and Industry (CORE X005) Building Belonging: Navigating Cultural Complexities (CORE X006) When applying, you will be invited to rank, in order of preference, the three courses for which you would like to be considered. Before crafting your cover letter, please review the Expectations of Commons Workshop Facilitators Semester 1 2027 . Eligibility We seek registrations of interest from folk who: Demonstrate a postgraduate qualification (e.g. Graduate Certificate, Graduate Diploma, Master's degree, or doctoral qualification), or equivalent professional expertise relevant to the course context. Work collaboratively and contribute positively to a teaching team. Use , or demonstrate a willingness to develop capability in using, a range of digital tools that support student learning. Facilitate interactive and inclusive learning environments through strong communication and facilitation skills. Bring previous Common Core teaching experience, although this is desirable rather than essential Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, gender identities, and disciplinary backgrounds. Dates to keep in mind, our Semester 1 onboarding day will be held on Wednesday, 10 February 2027 , with semester commencing in the week beginning 22 February 2027 . Please note – Please note that while registration on the Casual/Sessional Staff Register allows you to be considered for opportunities, it does not guarantee that employment will be offered. Please click on the Apply Now button and upload: Your current CV A 2-page cover letter outlining: Your motivation for joining the Common Core. Your motivation for applying for the course(s) that you have selected. Your interest in and suitability for online Commons Workshops, should these opportunities be available. Your interest in and suitability for co-facilitating large, multi-teacher, on-Campus Commons Workshops, should these opportunities be available. Submit your application by 11.30pm, Sunday, 06 December 2026. If you have any questions, please contact commoncore@adelaide.edu.au . Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 08a9cf19 Last Name (required) fc71197d Email (required) 27007a0a Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 949f303c Last Name (required) 8141b3ec Email (required) ee363440 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Stores Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Health Exciting opportunity to contribute to a dynamic team supporting education, research and operational excellence. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 5cb63727 Last Name (required) b351c137 Email (required) 921d1900 Job Alert cc69cd71 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Casual Campaign Casual Campaign Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio Academic Academic Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
