    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/stores-assistant-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Stores Assistant",
      "description": "Stores Assistant - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Stores Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training HEO3 Fixed term - Full-time HEO3 Position Description Based in the College of Health at Adelaide University Full-time, fixed term contract until December 2027 Salary: HEO 3, $47,006 - $74,733 plus 17% superannuation At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it's a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia's future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As the Stores Assistant, you will play a vital role in supporting the College of Health's teaching, research and technical activities through the efficient management of the central store. Your work will ensure staff and students have timely access to the equipment and consumables they need to deliver outstanding educational and research outcomes. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Team Lead, Technical Services, this position sits within the Specialist Facilities and Technical Services team in the College of Health. The team provides essential operational support that enables high-quality teaching, research and practical learning experiences across the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the College of Health . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys variety, organisation and helping others. You'll work with a broad range of staff, students, suppliers and service providers while balancing customer service, stock management, equipment coordination and administration responsibilities in a busy and collaborative environment. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Certificate III in Warehouse Operations, relevant tertiary qualification, or an equivalent combination of experience and training. Experience in a customer-focused service environment with the ability to adapt to changing priorities. Demonstrated financial administration and accurate record-keeping skills. Experience using Microsoft Office applications, including Excel. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders. Experience managing stock, equipment, purchasing or logistics activities will be highly regarded. Special requirements You may be required to work outside standard hours, including evenings or weekends This role may involve manual handling, working at heights or in confined spaces Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: Your current CV A cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 3 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493438 ): Amra Delibasic Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/veterinary-nurse-team-lead-roseworthy-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse Team Lead",
      "description": "Veterinary Nurse Team Lead - Roseworthy, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Veterinary Nurse Team Lead Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 Education & Training Farming, Animals & Conservation Continuing - Full-time HEO5 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Veterinary Nurse Team Lead – Small Animal Hospital Based at Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital, Roseworthy Campus Full-time Continuing position Leading the ECC nursing team in a 24/7 rotating roster, some participation in ECC nursing roster will be required penalties and shift loading apply Salary Range: (HEO 5) $84,498 to $93,955 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Lead and mentor a dedicated veterinary nursing team in a modern, accredited teaching hospital providing general practice, specialist and emergency care. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters We are seeking an experienced Veterinary Nurse Team Lead to combine advanced clinical nursing skills with strong leadership and team development in our busy, modern veterinary teaching hospital. You will lead and support the nursing team, coordinate daily workloads and patient admissions and discharges, and work collaboratively with veterinary clinicians and client services staff to deliver exceptional patient care. Alongside mentoring team members, identifying professional development opportunities and supporting the clinical education and mentorship of future veterinary professionals, you will remain actively involved in clinical procedures, surgery, diagnostics and patient monitoring. You will also contribute to maintaining high clinical standards, improving processes and ensuring the hospital operates safely and efficiently. This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to animal welfare, foster a supportive and high-performing team, and help shape the next generation of veterinary professionals. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role sits within the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital team in the College of Science and reports to the Hospital Manager. You will join the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital (RVH) at Roseworthy, working closely with the Hospital Manager, Practice Coordinator, fellow Nursing Team Lead, veterinary clinicians and support staff to coordinate daily operations and maintain high clinical standards. The hospital provides general practice, specialist and 24-hour emergency services, while also supporting the clinical education of veterinary and veterinary technology students. In this leadership role, you will provide guidance, direction, coaching and professional development support to help build a skilled, collaborative and high-performing nursing team. You will receive guidance and support from the Hospital Manager and work closely with veterinary clinicians, client services staff, nursing team members, students undertaking clinical placements, external clients and referring veterinarians. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for an experienced veterinary nurse who enjoys combining hands-on clinical work with leadership, mentoring and operational coordination. You will work in a collaborative, fast-paced clinical environment where teamwork, communication and a commitment to high standards of animal care are essential. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Qualifications Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing, or a Bachelor of Veterinary Technology, with 5 years’ experience Experience Experience leading and supporting a team in a veterinary or clinical environment Proven ability in veterinary nursing support during procedures, examinations, and surgeries Proven ability to maintain high standards of principles and practices in all areas of veterinary nursing Proven ability to establish effective working relationships within a team Proven ability in written and oral communication for managing professional and operational relationships Proven ability in organisational and time management skills Proven ability as a proficient user of Microsoft Office suite and relevant clinical databases Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Wednesday 4 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493632 ) : Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 580085b5 Last Name (required) b6d91f5c Email (required) d8c0cee4 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) be8bceb0 Last Name (required) 8bc58d67 Email (required) e038eb1d Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) ea71f1f9 Last Name (required) 5158e208 Email (required) 92bb5bb1 Job Alert 8426e84c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education & Training Farming, Animals & Conservation Education & Training Farming, Animals & Conservation Locations Roseworthy, SA, Australia Roseworthy, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Science College of Science Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
