    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/data-engineer-sql-specialist-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Data Engineer, SQL Specialist",
      "description": "Data Engineer, SQL Specialist - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Data Engineer, SQL Specialist Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training HEO7 Fixed term - Full-time Position Description Based in the Business Intelligence team at the City West campus Full-time 24 month fixed term contract Salary Range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Apply your advanced SQL expertise to deliver enterprise data solutions and analytics At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters We are seeking an experienced SQL specialist to design, develop and optimise enterprise data solutions that support data-driven decision-making across Adelaide University. Advanced SQL skills are essential. You will develop and maintain data pipelines, transformations, models and reporting datasets, ensuring trusted and accessible data is available to support strategic and operational outcomes. Experience with cloud data platforms, data engineering, ETL/ELT pipelines and modern analytics platforms is desirable; however, on-the-job training can be provided for the right candidate. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Business Intelligence team within the Performance, Data and Insights Function and is aligned to the Corporate Portfolio within the University. The Data Engineer will work most closely with the Chief Data and Analytics Officer, Director, Business Intelligence, and the IT and Finance teams. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Advanced SQL expertise, including complex query development, optimisation, troubleshooting and data transformation. Experience in data manipulation, preparation, and integration Experience in designing, developing, and supporting data pipelines, models, and processes Proficiency in data management and business intelligence concepts and practices Experience with data manipulation tools and/or programming languages such as SQL, DBT, Microsoft Fabric, Oracle Data Integrator (ODI). Experience in stakeholder engagement, expectations, and relationship management Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 8 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493655): Alexandra Koszegi Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
