    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/nhmrc-grant-funded-postdoctoral-research-associate-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "NHMRC Grant-Funded Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "NHMRC Grant-Funded Postdoctoral Research Associate - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me NHMRC Grant-Funded Postdoctoral Research Associate Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Based in the College of Health, Adelaide Health and Medical Sciences (AHMS) Building Full-time, fixed- term contract for 12 months Salary range: (Level A) $82,838 to $$111,384 per annum, plus 17% superannuation At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters We invite applications from highly motivated early-career researchers to join our multidisciplinary research team as an NHMRC grant funded Research Associate. This position is ideal for a researcher seeking to further develop their expertise in stem cell biology, developmental biology, epigenetics, and gene regulation within a collaborative and intellectually stimulating research environment. The Research Associate will undertake independent and collaborative research projects focused on stem cell and organoid biology, contributing to studies investigating mechanisms of gene regulation, cellular differentiation, development, and disease progression. About Adelaide Centre for Epigenetics (ACE) Our research program seeks to understand how epigenetic and transcriptional regulatory networks control cellular identity, differentiation, and tissue development in health and disease. We utilise cutting-edge molecular and cellular biology approaches combined with advanced 2D and 3D stem cell culture systems, organoid models, functional genomics, and in vivo models to investigate fundamental biological processes relevant to development, cancer, and human disease. The successful candidate will join a collaborative team of researchers working across stem cell biology, developmental biology, epigenetics, cancer biology, and translational research, with access to state-of-the-art research infrastructure and opportunities to engage with national and international collaborators. Our people This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to internationally competitive research at the interface of stem cell biology, development, epigenetics, and disease modelling. The successful candidate will have access to advanced cell culture, imaging, genomics, and bioinformatics infrastructure, while working within a collaborative environment that supports scientific excellence, professional development, and career progression. You will be part of a research team committed to understanding fundamental mechanisms of cellular identity and development, translating these discoveries into new insights into human health and disease, and fostering the next generation of research leaders. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience Qualifications: Completion of a PhD in epigenetics or molecular and cellular biology, and/or equivalent professional experience. To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research, including leading research, where applicable in cancer systems and/or developmental biology including neurodevelopment. Experience in the use of complex stem cell and organoid culture systems. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to communicate within the team, across disciplines and with collaborators. High level organisational skills, including the ability to prioritise and manage workload within a busy environment and meet competing deadlines Demonstrated rational problem solving and analytical skills. Experience with a diverse range of molecular and cellular biology techniques, including but not limited to: Tissue/cell culture, Western Blot, immunofluorescence, techniques and analysis relating to epigenetics, transcription factor biology and regulation of gene expression, animal handling and knowledge of animal ethics. Involvement in professional activity and a commitment to ongoing learning. Clear record of driving to success all aspects of a research project, including experimental design, execution, and writing of manuscripts. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re interested in the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Monday 23 November 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493397) : Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Appointment is subject to a satisfactory National Police Check (NPC) being obtained and maintained. #LI-DNI #S-DN I Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-project-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Project Officer",
      "description": "Senior Project Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Project Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training HEO7 Fixed term - Part-time HEO7 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Integrity and Safer Community function at the City East campus Part-time (0.8 FTE), fixed term 12-month contract Salary range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Coordinate projects that support the prevention of, and response to, gender-based violence, working with international students to develop culturally appropriate, trauma-informed resources. This role is suited to someone with experience working in the gender-based violence and sexual harm space, who can engage students in meaningful, respectful conversations on sensitive topics while building trusted relationships with students from diverse cultural backgrounds. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team The Safer Community Unit is a centralised unit with responsibility for preventing and responding to harmful behaviours, including gender-based violence and racism. The Unit creates a space where individuals, including staff and students, can raise complaints or disclosures about conduct concerns in a safe, confidential and supportive environment. Visit the AU website to learn more about Corporate . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience coordinating projects in a complex environment Experience managing project documentation, schedules, and reporting Proven ability to engage and collaborate with diverse stakeholders, particularly those from diverse cultural backgrounds Experience in risk and issue management within project delivery Familiarity with compliance requirements in a university or similar setting Commitment to continuous improvement and service excellence Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Build on your career with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role and the relevant experience you can bring to the position, highlighting any previous community engagement experience or work with international students. The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Monday 2 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493485) : Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Pursuant to the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (the Act) and the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Regulations 2019 (the Regulations), this position has been deemed prescribed. This role will require the successful candidate to hold a current Working with Children Check. Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 36907440 Last Name (required) d2a89383 Email (required) db43f1b2 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 2b2bc902 Last Name (required) b265297d Email (required) 302319a9 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who a