    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/pay-auditing-specialist-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Pay Auditing Specialist",
      "description": "Pay Auditing Specialist - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Pay Auditing Specialist Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO7 Human resources Fixed term - Full-time Position Description Based in in People & Culture at the City West Campus Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract Salary Range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Every pay run matters. In this role, you’ll help ensure Adelaide University employees are paid accurately and compliantly by identifying payroll risks, strengthening controls, and driving continuous improvement. Your expertise will provide confidence in payroll processes, support regulatory compliance, and deliver meaningful assurance that protects both staff and the University. Working across payroll, risk, audit and compliance teams, you’ll turn insights into action and help build a culture of accuracy, accountability and trust. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team As part of the Quality and Compliance team, you’ll join a collaborative group of professionals committed to strengthening governance, compliance, payroll integrity, and continuous improvement across the University. Working closely with stakeholders across People and Culture, the team drives best-practice payroll governance, identifies opportunities for improvement, and helps ensure employees are paid accurately and in accordance with legislative and policy requirements. Through a strong focus on assurance, service excellence, and continuous improvement, the team delivers meaningful outcomes that build trust, reduce risk, and support both staff and the broader University community. Visit the AU website to learn more about People & Culture. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. The ideal candidate for this position is an analytical and detail-oriented payroll professional with experience in payroll audit, compliance, and risk management. They have a keen eye for identifying issues, improving controls, and ensuring payroll accuracy and legislative compliance. A strong communicator and collaborator, they build effective relationships across teams, using data-driven insights to influence positive outcomes. Proactive and solutions-focused, they are committed to continuous improvement and delivering trusted payroll assurance services. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience working in payroll functions with demonstrated understanding of payroll processes and controls Experience working in internal audit, assurance or related roles supporting audit and compliance activities Proven ability to analyse complex data and apply payroll and human resources control frameworks Proven ability to produce high-quality documentation and reports in line with audit standards Experience working with risk and control frameworks and handling sensitive information appropriately Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter the online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30p m Monday 9 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493599 ) : Emma Kelvin , Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand? Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. Common Core Opportunities (Casual) – Semester 1, 2027 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Common Core are a defining feature of the Adelaide University curriculum architecture and a flagship component of our collective commitment to transformative education. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
