    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/technical-support-assistant-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Technical Support Assistant",
      "description": "Technical Support Assistant - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Technical Support Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO3 Continuing - Full-time HEO3 Position Description Based in the College of Science at Adelaide University Full-time continuing opportunity commencing 15 February 2027 Salary Range: $71,093 - $80,010 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it's a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia's future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Please note, this successful candidate will be expected to commence into this position on 15 February 2027. Work that matters As a Technical Support Assistant, you will play a vital role in enabling high-quality research and teaching by preparing laboratory media and solutions, maintaining equipment and facilities, and ensuring safe, efficient laboratory operations. Your work directly supports researchers, academics and students in delivering scientific discovery and innovation. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Manager, Technical Services, Biological Sciences, this role is part of the Specialist Facilities and Technical Services team within the College of Science. The team provides essential technical expertise, laboratory support and facility management services that enable research excellence and teaching outcomes across the University. Visit the Adelaide University website to learn more about the College of Science. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys a hands-on laboratory environment and takes pride in delivering high-quality technical services. You will work with a diverse range of stakeholders across research and teaching environments, contributing to safe, efficient and compliant laboratory operations every day. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU. Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Certificate IV Level qualification (or equivalent) in Laboratory Operations, Life Sciences, or a related discipline with relevant work-related experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or training. Experience preparing, dispensing and sterilising media and laboratory solutions. Experience with aseptic techniques, autoclaving and sterilisation services. Understanding of laboratory-based research environments and the needs of active research groups. Proven ability to work independently and collaboratively with a strong customer service focus. Experience using computer systems and maintaining accurate records, inventory and transaction data. Special requirements You may be required to work outside standard hours, including evenings or weekends You may be required to work across multiple campuses or remotely, depending on operational needs Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Monday 16 November 2026. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493423): Amra Delibasic Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Lecturer (B) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Pharmacy and Biomedical Sciences This Teaching and Research position provides an exciting opportunity to work within a vibrant biomedical research environment based at the Adelaide Health and Medical Sciences building within the Discipline of Reproduction and Development. Senior Application Support Specialist (Collaboration & Productivity Platform) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Provide technical leadership and expert application support across collaboration platforms, delivering secure, reliable services and continuous improvement. Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-application-support-specialist-collaboration-productivity-platform-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Application Support Specialist (Collaboration & Productivity Platform)",
      "description": "Senior Application Support Specialist (Collaboration & Productivity Platform) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Application Support Specialist (Collaboration & Productivity Platform) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO8 Information Technology Continuing - Full-time Position Description Based in IT Research Enablement and Digital Business at the City/Mawson Lakes Campus Full-time, continuing position Salary Range: $121,744 - $135,754 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Reporting to the IT Product Manager, Collaboration and Productivity Tools, you will provide senior technical leadership across Adelaide University’s collaboration and productivity platforms, with a strong focus on Microsoft 365, including SharePoint, Teams, OneDrive, Power Platform and Microsoft Copilot. You will design, configure and continuously improve secure, reliable and maintainable solutions that make the University’s digital workplace simpler and more effective. Working collaboratively with business stakeholders, architects, technical teams and vendors, you will translate complex requirements into practical solutions, provide technical direction, contribute to solution and architecture decisions, undertake technical and design reviews, and resolve complex platform and security issues. You will help strengthen platform governance and lifecycle management, reduce duplication, improve integration and enable responsible use of AI, Copilot, automation and citizen development. Through technical leadership, mentoring, documentation and knowledge sharing, you will also build capability across the team and support the effective adoption of collaboration and productivity technologies across research, education and business operations. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of the Staff Experience Team within the Information Technology and Corporate Function. The Collaboration and Productivity Tools team enables exceptional collaboration and productivity across Adelaide University through stable, secure and well-governed digital platforms. We manage the lifecycle, incident triage, adoption and continuous improvement of Microsoft 365 Tools, SharePoint, Power Platform, OneDrive, Content Manager, Atlassian and other collaboration tools, helping teams work effectively while meeting the University’s security, information and records governance obligations. We also enable citizen developers and responsible AI activation across our platforms, helping staff adopt AI tools through practical guidance, knowledge sharing and capability building to simplify everyday work. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who combines strong technical expertise with excellent interpersonal skills and a genuine team-first approach. You will enjoy solving complex problems, collaborating with and supporting colleagues, sharing knowledge and ideas, and helping others build capability. You will be adaptable, accountable and approachable, with a strong commitment to delivering reliable, secure and continuously improving services that enhance the staff experience. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Minimum of five years’ hands-on experience administering, configuring, designing and supporting Microsoft 365 solutions within large and complex enterprise environments, with strong technical expertise across SharePoint, Microsoft Teams, OneDrive, Power Platform and Microsoft Copilot, including platform configuration, security, governance, integrations and the delivery of scalable and maintainable solutions. Ability to translate complex business requirements into innovative, secure and maintainable Microsoft 365 solutions, with experience delivering application and platform improvements, workflow automation and integrations across Microsoft 365 and Power Platform. Experience applying Microsoft Copilot, AI and intelligent automation to improve productivity, collaboration and user experience will be highly regarded. Senior technical leadership experience within a Microsoft 365 environment, including providing technical direction and mentoring to colleagues, contributing to solution and architecture decisions, undertaking technical and design reviews, investigating and triaging security incidents, and resolving complex platform issues. Designing, configuring, administering and continuously improving enterprise applications and services, including delivering platform upgrades and enhancements and working within Agile/Scrum delivery environments. Supporting broader collaboration, productivity and information management technologies such as Atlassian Confluence and Jira, Content Manager and related enterprise platforms. Existing specialist expertise in these technologies is welcomed but not essential. Ability to build effective relationships and work collaboratively with business stakeholders, architects, technical teams and vendors, translating technical concepts and complex issues into clear and practical advice. Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, with demonstrated experience developing technical documentation, sharing knowledge and providing practical guidance to technical and non-technical stakeholders. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University, Tirkangkaku now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Wednesday 11 November 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493609 ): Jessica De Lorenzo Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Lecturer (B) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Pharmacy and Biomedical Sciences This Teaching and Research position provides an exciting opportunity to work within a vibrant biomedical research environment based at the Adelaide Health and Medical Sciences building within the Discipline of Reproduction and Development. Technical Support Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Specialist Facilities and Technical Services - Science Prepare media and laboratory solutions, maintain technical facilities, and support research and teaching through safe, compliant laboratory operations. Administration Support Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success Provide high-quality administrative and operational support, acting as a key point of contact for internal and external stakeholders and helping ensure the smooth and effective delivery of day-to-day operations. Senior Software Engineer (Enterprise Service Management) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Information Technology Lead the design and delivery of secure, scalable ServiceNow solutions, providing technical leadership, development expertise and mentoring across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    }
